  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(103.82pt, 579.79pt, " refer to the signal and idler photons. This expression captures the essential feature of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 594.31pt, "polarization entanglement: although neither photon has a definite polarization on its own, any ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 608.86pt, "measurement performed on one instantly determines the polarization outcome of the other, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 623.5pt, "regardless of their spatial separation.  ")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 650.02pt, "Physically, the entanglement arises from the quantum indistinguishability of the possible ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 664.54pt, "down-conversion pathways inside the crystal. The pump photon may convert into either a pair of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 679.06pt, "horizontally polarized photons or a pair of vertically polarized photons. In the absence of any ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 693.696pt, "environmental information that could distinguish between these alternatives, the system is forced ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 708.216pt, "by quantum mechanics into a coherent superposition of both processes. This superposition is ")
]

