  #line-at(70.824pt, 298.97pt, "Also in case of the idler photon reflection, the signal photon collapses into the basis state with the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 313.49pt, "same polarization as that of the reflected idler photon. In other words, the idler photon is absorbed ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 328.37pt, "or reflected either in state ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(197.09pt, 328.37pt, "∣𝐻⟩")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(215.69pt, 328.37pt, " or ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(231.17pt, 328.37pt, "∣𝑉⟩")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(248.69pt, 328.37pt, ", it is dependent on optical properties of the reflected surface ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 342.89pt, "on the idler arm beam path. When the idler photon undergoes polarization-dependent loss or ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 357.41pt, "measurement, the conditional polarization statistics of the entangled signal photon reflect the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 372.05pt, "same preference, and the joint detection statistics exhibit corresponding correlations [23]. The ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 386.81pt, "signal photon remains in the polarization state given by Eq. (1), and its ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(408.19pt, 386.81pt, "𝐻")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(416.47pt, 386.81pt, "/")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(419.59pt, 386.81pt, "𝑉")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(426.79pt, 386.81pt, " statistics are correlated ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 401.33pt, "with the reflectance of the coupled idler photon through coincidence measurements. Such ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 415.97pt, "entangled-state correlations have nothing in common with the  classical signal propagation and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 430.51pt, "can be exploited in the idler arm to detect rapid optical changes, for example those induced by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 445.03pt, "temperature variations. This fast and remote detection of dynamic optical properties is particularly ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 459.55pt, "suitable for the analysis of ultrashort laser pulse material ablation, where a simple bucket ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 474.07pt, "photodetector can be used on the idler side instead of a complex optical system. The bucket ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 488.71pt, "detector does not resolve the polarization state of the idler photon and serves solely as a trigger; ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 503.23pt, "however, a fixed polarization filter can be introduced at the detector to enhance filtering and isolate ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 517.75pt, "a selected polarization component. All polarization-resolved analysis is then performed remotely ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 532.27pt, "in the “clean” signal arm, where the detected data can be processed at high speed using an ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 546.91pt, "oscilloscope or FPGA module (Fig. 1). It should be noted that the proposed method does not ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 561.43pt, "provide a direct measurement of temperature; instead, it relies on calibration for a given material, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 575.95pt, "enabling the evaluation of temperature-dependent processes such as heat accumulation or phase ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 590.47pt, "transitions. ")
]

