  #line-at(70.824pt, 271.13pt, "Fig. 2. Time-resolved measurements from pump-probe reflectometry (PPR) of Al and AISI304 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 285.65pt, "during laser surface ablation (for experimental details see [14]). ")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 312.17pt, "After an ultrashort laser pulse, the surface temperature rapidly increases. The longer ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 326.69pt, "process of surface cooling is coming afterwards and can take several microseconds. In a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 341.33pt, "subsequent nanosecond-long interval after the laser pulse, several physical processes are ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 355.85pt, "activated, such as spallation and phase explosion, which initiate optical wave propagation. Then ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 370.37pt, "latent heat keeps the cooling process longer with other corresponding processes of surface ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 384.89pt, "reformation [1], [4], [5], [13], [14]. At the same time period, the ablation plume is spread out above ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.41pt, "the laser processed surface. It is difficult to separate the IR thermal radiation from the laser-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 414.05pt, "processed surface, as it contains several components: plasma emission, near-infrared thermal ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 428.59pt, "radiation from the ablated material, and infrared thermal radiation from the post-ablated surface. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 443.11pt, "The influence of the mentioned effects will be suppressed by detection of a reflected beam with ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 457.63pt, "idler photons, which are entangled with the signal photons on the remote beam path. In our Qiskit ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 472.27pt, "model, the reflection of the idler photons is simulated using the wavelength-dependent real and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 486.79pt, "imaginary components of the refractive index.  ")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 513.31pt, "A rigorous derivation linking reflectivity to coincidence statistics is beyond the scope of this ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 527.83pt, "work. Instead, we use a phenomenological approach in which the effect is captured via reflection ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 542.35pt, "of idler photons entangled with the remote signal arm. In the Qiskit model, this reflection is ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 556.99pt, "described using time-dependent complex refractive index components n(t) and k(t), obtained by ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 571.51pt, "fitting pump–probe reflectance data from J. Winter et al. [15] and interpolated to the 810 nm idler ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 586.03pt, "wavelength. The model therefore relies on experimentally validated optical parameters and they ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 600.58pt, "were derived from pump–probe experimental data and interpolated to match the 810 nm idler ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 615.22pt, "wavelength [14]: ")
