  #line-at(70.824pt, 434.23pt, "is the number of time points. This metric provides a direct measure of the temperature evaluation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 448.75pt, "error in physical units (°C) and enables a consistent comparison between the two reconstruction ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 463.39pt, "approaches. ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(88.824pt, 516.31pt, "4. Discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.82pt, 542.95pt, "The presented results have shown that entangled photons can be used for fast detection ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 557.47pt, "of surface temperature changes. In the simulation, the periodicity of the entangled pairs generation ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 572.11pt, "of around 50 ps was used. According to the described principle, the temperature changes during ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 586.87pt, "rapid surface heating were evaluated from the ratio between ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(367.15pt, 586.87pt, "𝐻")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(375.43pt, 586.87pt, "- and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(403.63pt, 586.87pt, "𝑉")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(410.83pt, 586.87pt, "-state counts in the remote ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 601.42pt, "signal arm, while the idler photons were used as a coincidence trigger (Eq. 5). The evaluation of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 616.06pt, "absolute temperature based on experimental data with pulsed ellipsometry measurements [14] ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 630.58pt, "gave realistic results. In principle the calibration of the remote temperature evaluation with ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 645.1pt, "entanglement photons can be done by preliminary measurements on a hot plate of the used ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 659.62pt, "material. Due to the quantised character of the entanglement photon detection it is impossible to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 674.26pt, "evaluate polarization anisotropy just by one event and it is needed to have some statistical ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 688.78pt, "window. The width of the used window was equal to 40 ns and it gives the time shift of the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 703.296pt, "temperature rise of around 200 ns and SNR around 10 dB. The statistical character of such ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 718.056pt, "measurement imposes a limitation on the time resolution and binary nature of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.14pt, 718.056pt, "𝐻")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(475.42pt, 718.056pt, "- and ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
