  #line-at(513.58pt, 718.056pt, "-state ")
]

// arXiv source page 15
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(528.94pt, 740.976pt, "15 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 81pt, "output vectors. The application of neural network algorithms to this type of data has demonstrated ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 95.66pt, "improved precision. For a model with 600 statistical estimation bins and more than seven million ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 110.18pt, "trainable parameters, the temporal shift of the temperature rise is approximately 8 ns, while the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 124.7pt, "signal-to-noise ratio exceeds 26 dB. Such a difference of the binary data processing is explained ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 139.22pt, "by the basic principle of the discrete measurements. This can be explained as shown in Fig. 6, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 154.1pt, "where absorption of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(171.5pt, 154.1pt, "𝑝")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(177.74pt, 154.1pt, "-polarized photons is higher, but it also results in increased noise. It is just ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 168.62pt, "by more rarely appearing of “1” state detection in comparison to untriggered photons. As a result, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 183.14pt, "the measured data contain a more randomly distributed pattern of “1” bits within an array of “0” ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 197.78pt, "bits. That is why the analytical method of such data processing has not worked properly and MLP ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 212.3pt, "method becomes beneficial. ")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 238.82pt, "It should be emphasized that classical temperature-detection techniques offer several ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 253.58pt, "advantages. These include direct access to the complex refractive index ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(432.43pt, 253.58pt, "𝑛+ 𝑖𝑘")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(461.98pt, 253.58pt, " through mature ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 268.25pt, "modeling approaches with sub-millidegree precision in ellipsometry, and reflection-free ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 282.77pt, "temperature measurement in pyrometry. But the entangled photons polarization anisotropy ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 297.29pt, "detection has great advantage in background rejection via coincidences. Only idler detections that ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 311.81pt, "arrive within the coincidence window of an entangled signal photon are counted. This suppresses ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 326.45pt, "the stray light, furnace glow, and detector dark counts far better than classical ellipsometry or ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 340.97pt, "pyrometry (which integrate all photons hitting the detector). The next feature is the heralded ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 355.49pt, "detection with known arrival times. The signal photon “announces” the idler and picosecond (or ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 370.01pt, "sub-ns) coincidence gates can be used, even when single-photon pulses are weak. The next ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 384.65pt, "benefit of the entangled photons application lies in the wavelength optimization for the metal ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 399.17pt, "reflectance for low-noise with high-QE detectors. Classical pyrometry is constrained by thermal-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 413.69pt, "emission spectral bands, whereas ellipsometry requires an intense probe beam and high-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 428.23pt, "sensitivity detectors at the probe wavelength. The discrete character of the entanglement photons ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 442.75pt, "polarization anisotropy detection has ultralow probe flux (non-perturbative). It gives higher SNR ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 457.39pt, "above backgrounds, orders-of-magnitude fewer photons than classical ellipsometry. It is ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 471.91pt, "especially important when additional heating or ablation must be avoided. Another distinctive ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 486.43pt, "feature of the H- to V-state ratio principle is its immunity to emissivity drift. In contrast to pyrometry, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 500.95pt, "in which temperature evaluation is sensitive to unknown or varying emissivity and view factors, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 515.59pt, "the proposed method is largely immune to these effects. Temperature evaluation with polarization ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 530.11pt, "anisotropy has the shot-noise suppression potential. With the correlated pairs and proper ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 544.63pt, "statistics, the classical shot-noise scaling is beaten for the same detected flux with improving ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 559.15pt, "precision per detected photon. It should be noted that the measured data are represented as a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 573.67pt, "long binary vector, for which classical analysis methods are not effective in extracting the signal. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 588.31pt, "On the other hand, the application of neural network analysis is able to extract implicit information ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 602.86pt, "for correct evaluation of thermal process dynamics. This is clearly seen by comparing the results ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 617.38pt, "of the sliding-window algorithm (Fig. 7) with those of the MLP data-processing model (Fig. 9).  ")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 643.9pt, "The reconstruction accuracy of the sliding-window method and the ML model was ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 658.54pt, "evaluated over 150 generated datasets with controlled accidental coincidence noise. The ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 673.06pt, "accidental contribution was varied up to approximately 95% of all detected coincidence events. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 687.58pt, "The resulting temperature evaluation error, quantified by RMSE (Section 3), is summarized in Fig. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 702.096pt, "10 as a function of the accidental fraction. Under near-ideal conditions, both methods reproduce ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 716.616pt, "the general temperature dynamics; however, the sliding-window approach exhibits significantly ")
]

