  #line-at(70.824pt, 139.22pt, "substantially lower errors of about 300 °C. At the highest tested noise level, corresponding to ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 153.86pt, "approximately 95% accidental coincidences (about 20 times more accidental than true ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 168.38pt, "coincidence events), the sliding-window reconstruction exhibits both high error and large variability ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 182.9pt, "between datasets. In contrast, the ML-based approach remains comparatively robust, maintaining ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 197.42pt, "lower RMSE values and a much smaller spread of results. The behavior observed in Fig. 10 ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 211.94pt, "indicates that reconstruction based on local coincidence statistics is highly sensitive to accidental ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 226.58pt, "coincidences, whereas the neural-network model is better able to account for noise and preserve ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 241.1pt, "a physically meaningful temperature evolution over a broad range of measurement conditions. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 505.39pt, "Fig. 10. Temperature evaluation error (RMSE) as a function of accidental coincidence rate (false ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 519.91pt, "pairs per pulse): blue - for the ML-based and orange - sliding-window reconstruction methods. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 534.43pt, "The shaded regions indicate the standard deviation over the dataset. ")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 587.59pt, "The middle-sized ANN used in this work can be further improved by training with higher-")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 602.14pt, "resolution data or by switching to raw-data processing instead of statistical estimation bins. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 616.66pt, "However, in this case, the neural network would need to be adapted for GPU acceleration and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 631.18pt, "extended to a deeper architecture. It makes sense in the case of real applications where the output ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 645.82pt, "values are predefined for a narrow task. The goal of this work is to show an alternative method for ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 660.34pt, "temperature measurement based on quantum effects with binary data format processing. ")
  #line-at(106.82pt, 686.86pt, "Another possible approach to fast temperature evaluation using entangled photons is ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 701.376pt, "based on a hybrid methodology combined with discrete Fourier transform (DFT)-based data ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 716.016pt, "processing. In this scheme, coincidence detection is employed as a triggering mechanism together ")
]

