  #line-at(70.824pt, 81pt, "conditions. Although the MLP-based reconstruction exhibits reduced temporal resolution, it ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 95.66pt, "enables faster detection of temperature rise in the considered scenario. The robustness of the ML ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 110.18pt, "model against accidental coincidences was evaluated using RMSE as a function of noise level, ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 124.7pt, "demonstrating significantly higher stability compared to the sliding-window method. While the ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 139.22pt, "classical approach becomes unstable at high noise levels (up to 12% accidental pairs), the ML ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 153.86pt, "model maintains controlled error and lower variance. These results indicate that data-driven ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 168.38pt, "reconstruction can mitigate the impact of noise in entangled-photon-based measurements. A more ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 182.9pt, "detailed uncertainty analysis, including confidence intervals and kernel-based methods, may be ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 197.42pt, "considered in future work. The presented results suggest that neural-network-based processing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 211.94pt, "can extend the applicability of entangled-photon temperature measurements toward high-speed ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 226.58pt, "regimes. Further development may include the use of weak measurement schemes [33], where ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 241.1pt, "indirect measurements combined with neural-network-based reconstruction could provide ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 255.65pt, "improved sensitivity and resolution.")
